  "implemented": [
    "Core-only typed delegation.resume command uses the existing exact-replay Gateway identity and persistent receipt, with original Run ownership for recovery after later attempts or global disable; no public tool/CLI/API activation",
    "Preparation requires active authenticated parent, original direct-child ownership, current and frozen enabled/depth, current membership, canceled current attempt with cleanup acknowledged and no pending causal cleanup, original directory permission and exact original managed task digest",
    "Source frozen Runtime columns reuse the original Runtime consistency validator, and fresh Registry resolution revalidates logical target, saved permissions/model/custom API rather than selecting current member defaults",
    "Current accepted input must belong to the exact previous Run/epoch/Binding/generation, its unique-per-Run Manifest and nonempty native input/request digest. Earlier accepted attempts cannot qualify an unaccepted current attempt",
    "Preparation rejects active/recovering/unacknowledged Runs, prepared/unknown input, unresolved actions/approvals/checkpoints and known other-conversation Session writers. Original filesystem directory is observed outside the DB transaction; commit rechecks the prepared fingerprint",
    "One transaction advances current attempt/control and Conversation sequence/version by CAS, reuses the initial factory Run insertion algorithm, appends a new Run/Turn/attempt in the same child Conversation and emits metadata-only resumed event",
    "Original task Blob and old accepted delivery/Manifest remain unchanged. The new input is only the approved fixed delegation-resume.txt hint; optional reason appears only in approved interruptionContext and attempt storage",
    "Private delegationResume metadata freezes original Session/Binding/generation/source input and exact attempt identity. Missing metadata for a resume attempt is an error; the nullable compatibility key retains original adapter semantics",
    "Runtime launch/binding/rebind paths verify same Session and native compatibility; original shared fallback predicate forbids cold Session replacement only for these resume Runs. A storage error propagates and cannot become a durable ordinary refusal",
    "Registry re-resolution deliberately produces provisional native evidence. Resume queues the original frozen execution basis and relies on the original dispatch integrity/native-load pipeline. Compatible Runtime rebind is allowed when Session compatibility remains unchanged",
    "Pending160/210 migration extends only the existing attachment-auth guard version list to35, retaining all request digest/auth receipt conditions. Existing Context/profile guards still validate35 role tuples"
  ],
